CascadEffects Performance Platform
Waypoint 18 — Platform Authorization Foundation

Date: 2026-08-29

Milestone Status: COMPLETE — Platform Authorization Foundation

Overview

This milestone establishes the platform-level authorization foundation for CascadEffects.

The platform now distinguishes CascadEffects platform authority from organization-scoped roles and permissions. Platform Super Admins are represented through a dedicated platform membership model and can administer organizations without requiring an organization membership in each organization.

The existing organization Roles & Permissions architecture remains intact and is now complemented by a platform-level authority layer.

Completed Work

1. Created the platform_memberships database model.

2. Established the platform_role = super_admin authority model.

3. Added active/inactive platform membership state.

4. Added uniqueness protection for user/platform-role combinations.

5. Added platform membership indexes.

6. Added server-side isPlatformSuperAdmin() authorization resolution.

7. Added requirePlatformSuperAdmin() enforcement helper.

8. Updated organization permission resolution so an active Platform Super Admin is recognized before organization membership checks.

9. Preserved the existing organization authorization chain for non-platform users.

10. Updated the server Supabase client to use the request-scoped authenticated session.

11. Repaired Supabase migration history for the renamed Teams and Users/Memberships migrations.

12. Applied migration 20260829_create_platform_memberships.sql to the remote database.

13. Verified local and remote migration histories are synchronized.

14. Verified the platform_memberships table exists remotely.

15. Verified the application build passes.

16. Verified git diff --check reports no actual whitespace errors.

Architecture Decisions

• Platform Super Admin is a platform-level authority and is not an organization role.

• Platform membership is modeled separately from organization_memberships.

• Platform Super Admin authority does not require membership in every organization.

• Organization permissions continue to resolve through Organization Membership → Membership Roles → Roles → Role Permissions → Permissions.

• Platform authority is evaluated before organization membership authorization.

• The organizationId still identifies the organization being administered.

• The current implementation is a foundation and does not constitute complete production authorization.

• Production RLS and comprehensive authorization enforcement remain separate future security milestones.

• The server Supabase client is request-scoped and preserves the authenticated session through Next.js cookies.

• Client components must not import the server authorization infrastructure.

