• platform_memberships_active_idx

Migration history is synchronized through migration 20260829.

Documentation Updated

This Waypoint records the completion of the Platform Authorization Foundation milestone.

Current Platform Decisions remain authoritative. Production authorization, production RLS, Runtime security boundaries, Assignment Subject Validation, and Performance Instance Relationship Integrity remain future work.

Technical Debt

• The authorization layer currently performs multiple sequential Supabase queries and should not be prematurely optimized before production authorization requirements are finalized.

• Production authorization enforcement is not yet comprehensive across every UI, server service, API route, and database policy.

• Production Row Level Security remains outstanding.

• Assignment Subject Validation remains outstanding.

• Performance Instance Relationship Integrity remains outstanding.

• The current Platform Super Admin model intentionally supports only super_admin and may be generalized later if a real platform-role requirement emerges.

Next Session

Review the latest Waypoint, Platform Decisions, and Platform Backlog before implementation.

The next architectural focus should be the production tenant authorization and security boundary, with particular attention to authenticated identity, organization membership, role assignment, permission assignment, requested organization context, resource ownership, server/service enforcement, API enforcement, and database/RLS enforcement.

Do not rebuild the Builder or Runtime foundations.

Milestone Status

COMPLETE

Platform Authorization Foundation is complete and verified.

The platform now has a dedicated platform-level membership model and server-side Super Admin authorization foundation.

This milestone does NOT mark Production Authorization or Production RLS as complete.